Track 3: "Did the Projectionist Cut the Wire?"
- Story & Context: Years after the collective abandoned their projection booth to the coastal fog, squatters exploring the decommissioned Skrunda cinema complex unearthed a locked flight case containing an unlabelled cassette wound with silver splicing tape. Local lore claimed that during their final underground performance, Soren and Mina had deliberately cut the theatre's grounding wire, allowing the 142-BPM half-time kick-drops to violently vibrate the projector until the glass lens cracked and showered the audience in warm sparks. Scratched with a razor blade directly onto the tape's plastic shell was the track's final, lingering hook: "They erased the territory but the rapture won’t dissolve."
